id: pm-bukwmy
title: Reject repository-local test scratch roots before sandbox fixtures can mutate the real Git workspace
description: "Setting TMPDIR inside the checkout makes disposable test fixtures inherit the real Git root and ancestor tracker. Observed coverage fixtures replaced repository .gitattributes and .gitignore managed sections and invalidated no-Git assertions. The package-owned test runner must reject this configuration before starting build or Vitest, including symlink aliases of the checkout; external scratch roots remain supported."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-08T05:41:23.494Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T06:56:00.537Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T06:55:59.820Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T06:55:59.820Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Repository-local and symlink-aliased temporary roots fail before child execution with a clear remediation.; External temporary roots still run sandboxed test and coverage modes without changing real Git or tracker state.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "The test runner rejects checkout-local scratch directories, including symlink aliases, before build or fixture execution. Real vector, SDK and socket fixtures use owned portable temporary paths."
expected_result: Prevent fixtures from discovering and modifying the real repository through a checkout-local temporary root; retain safe external-root execution.
actual_result: "93 linked regression tests pass, including the runner negative controls and portable fixtures. The full suite with four workers and exact coverage passes using an external scratch root. No lock threshold or coverage threshold was weakened."
